    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "Open or closed vowel",
     "texto": [
      "**É** and **ó** usually represent open vowels, as in **pé** and **avó**. **Ê** and **ô** represent closed vowels, as in **avô** and **pôr**. The grave accent on **à** has a different job: it marks a contraction.",
      "Compare **avó** (grandmother) and **avô** (grandfather); **pode** (can) and **pôde** (could); **por** (by / for) and **pôr** (to put)."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "The unstressed vowel",
     "texto": [
      "In European Portuguese, some unstressed vowels are reduced a lot when spoken. This pronunciation variation doesn't change the spelling of the word."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
